  "cleanText": "Solution home \n\t\tSelf Assessment \n\t\tSelf Assessment FAQs\n\n### HMRC Connect error messages\n\n\t\t\tPrint\n\n\tModified on: Fri, 9 Feb, 2024 at  9:24 AM\n\n\t\tHMRC connect doesn't always pull through information from HMRC, this could be for a number of reasons, the error messages are shown below:\n\nCode : NOT_FOUND\n\nMessage : Resource was not found\n\nError Details: NOT_FOUND: \n\nThere is no data available from HMRC for the given UTR number and the tax year.\n\nData is only available once PAYE reconciliation has completed\n\nReconciliation starts on or around 6th June and runs for around one million individuals per working night. It is usually completed by the end of November. Unfortunately it is not possible to know when reconciliation will be completed for a specific individual.\n\nCode : SA_UTR_INVALID\n\nMessage : The provided SA UTR is invalid\n\nError Details : SA_UTR_INVALID\n\nThe UTR number is invalid.\n\nCode : INVALID_CREDENTIALS\n\nMessage : Invalid Authentication information provided\n\nError Details : There seems to be an issue with the authentication, the token is invalid or has expired.  Please click here to reauthorise\n\nIf you would like further clarification please raise a support ticket.\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tDid you find it helpful?\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tYes\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tNo\n\nSend feedback\tSorry we couldn't be helpful. Help us improve this article with your feedback.",
